{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789783134,"nonce":"rI26RdqEVBJsXwHPpIkfi6/zyqg=","title":"auto_vectorize took a recurrence for a reduction and left invariant operands scalar","message":"A header phi with init 0 and body update `phi + expr` was classified as a\nreduction accumulator even when the body read the phi elsewhere (`x += c`\nwith `x` also feeding other arithmetic), and an operand from outside the\nloop was used unsplatted in vector arithmetic. Exposed once scalarized\ntuples gave such loops scalar phis: the interpreter rejected the mixed\nvector/scalar fadd, and the lane-split recurrence would have doubled its\ninitial value on the horizontal add.\n\nFix: an accumulator is read only by its own update and the update only by\nthe phi; a loop with no vector load or store is not vectorized; operands\nstill scalar after substitution are splatted.","files":null}]}